          "status": "needs-review",
          "text": "Description: Given the witness descriptions and investigation elements, the hypothesis of observing celestial lanterns appears very probable. Due to the two independent testimonies, the consistency of this case is high (0.8): the reality of the phenomenon is undoubted, even if it is not certain that the observations were simultaneous: it could be an uncertainty regarding the observation time, or a second release from the same location. The strangeness of the case is low (0.3) because the described phenomenon closely resembles a well-known phenomenon. The GEIPAN classifies this case as \"B\": very probable observation of celestial lanterns, also known as Thai lanterns. This case could be classified as A if the potential release authors could be identified.",
